{
	title: 'Find previews the selected row beside the results',
	spec: 'When the Find dialog is wide (web: viewport from 1200px; terminal: box interior from 160 columns), a preview pane sits right of the results. It shows the selected row card among its neighbors in history order (3 before, 3 after), drawn as transcript cards by the client own transcript renderer (web: Card, with card id links to the card in its tab; terminal: item lines), the web marking every query match and outlining the hit card, scrolled so the hit sits about a third down. A tab row previews its best-evidence card the same way; a tab row without card evidence (title or cwd match, recent tabs) previews its last cards. The previous preview stays until the next arrives: the pane never blanks between selections. Narrow dialogs show no pane. The worker answers the find-preview command with a find-preview event holding the history records, read by the byte offsets the find index stores; a failure shows in the pane.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Previews read neighbors by docs rowid within the session (history insertion order); about 3-5 ms on the real index, so no extra SQLite index or version bump. The web dialog wraps the list and pane in .body, display: contents for other modals.',
		'Preview pane wrapper is .split: Card has its own .body class, so a .Picker .body rule leaks into preview cards.'
	],
	needs: ['yhm'],
	foldInto: ['6m']
